values ('bbbb0005-0000-4000-8000-000000000013', 'en', null, 'A History of Science', 'How humanity learned to ask nature questions and trust the answers, from Babylonian star tables to the double helix. The itinerary runs through ancient Greece, the Islamic Golden Age, the Scientific Revolution, and the modern physics and biology that followed. Structure and figures adapted from the History of science article on Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia (CC BY-SA 4.0).', null, 'foundations', 59, true, 'humanities', '{}')
on conflict (id) do nothing;

